cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Circadian timing and amplitude define distinct relationships across human metabolic tissues"
message: "If you use this software, please cite both the software and the accompanying manuscript."
type: software
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-14
abstract: >-
  Code to infer circadian phase and amplitude from single transcriptomic samples and to measure
  coupling between two tissues of the same individual, separating the timing and the amplitude of
  the rhythm. Includes the validation against a controlled laboratory protocol with recorded
  sampling times, and the analysis of the response to metabolic perturbation.
keywords:
  - circadian
  - inter-tissue coupling
  - insulin resistance
  - skeletal muscle
  - adipose tissue
  - transcriptomics
